PDF extraction
•	Implemented using UglyToad.PdfPig (installed prerelease packages in environment).
•	Page-preserving extraction: the ingestion tool opens each PDF and reads per-page text via PdfPig API, then feeds pages into KnowledgeIngestionService for cleaning & chunking.
Chunking strategy
•	KnowledgeIngestionService:
•	Per-page cleaning (normalize whitespace, collapse extra line breaks).
•	Chunking by max char length with attempt to break at sentence boundaries.
•	Deterministic chunk IDs via SHA256(documentId|pageNumber|chunkIndex)
Deterministic IDs and idempotency
•	KnowledgeChunk.CreateDeterministicId(documentId, pageNumber, chunkIndex) produces hex SHA256 id.
•	KnowledgeIngestor upserts chunks using that id, so re-running the tool will update existing docs instead of creating duplicates.
KnowledgeIngestor usage
•	Build and run:
•	dotnet build tools/KnowledgeIngestor
•	dotnet run --project tools/KnowledgeIngestor
•	The tool:
•	Reads configuration from appsettings.json and environment variables
•	Locates knowledge/*.pdf
•	Extracts pages, chunks, calls OpenAI embeddings REST per batch, and upserts to Azure Search
•	Prints counts per document and totals
Configuration keys (set via appsettings or user-secrets / env vars)
•	AzureAiSearch:Endpoint — Azure Cognitive Search endpoint (e.g., https://<resource>.search.windows.net)
•	AzureAiSearch:ApiKey — admin/query API key for Azure Cognitive Search
•	AzureAiSearch:IndexName — index name (e.g., nova-banking-knowledge-index)
•	AzureAiSearch:EmbeddingDeployment — embedding deployment name (same as OpenAI deployment name)
•	AzureAiSearch:OpenAiEndpoint — Azure OpenAI resource endpoint (e.g., https://<resource>.openai.azure.com)
•	AzureAiSearch:OpenAiApiKey — Azure OpenAI API key
•	Alternative: set AzureOpenAI:Endpoint and AzureOpenAI:ApiKey; ServiceCollectionExtensions wires these into options.
